-- title:
--   Locally constant frame coordinates for action, level and generator
-- statement:
--   Setting. Let $q,q'$ be primes, let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$, and let `hB` assert `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q q'`, i.e. that $a>0$ or $b>0$ and that, for every height-one prime $v$ of the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}$, the completed algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division algebra (every nonzero element is a unit) exactly when $v$ contains $q$ or $q'$. Let $\Lambda\subseteq\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is a maximal order (`hΛ`: an order maximal among orders for inclusion), let $\iota\colon\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\to M_2(\mathbb{R})$ be an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map (`hι`), and assume $q'\neq q$. Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid N$, $q'\nmid N$ and $N$ squarefree, and let $R\subseteq\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be an Eichler order of level $N$ (an intersection $\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ of two maximal orders whose relative index in $\Lambda_1$ is $N$) with $R\le\Lambda$.
--
--   The uniformisation package over $\mathbb{C}$. A map $E\mapsto\mathrm{latt}(E)$ assigns to each fake elliptic curve $E$ for $(\Lambda,N)$ over $\mathbb{C}$ a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{C}^2$, and $e$ assigns to each such $E$ a bijection between the $\mathbb{C}$-points of $E$ over the identity of $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{C}$ (sections of `E.f`) and $\mathbb{C}^2/\mathrm{latt}(E)$. The hypotheses on this package are: `hL1`, that $\mathrm{latt}(E)$ is the $\mathbb{Z}$-span of an $\mathbb{R}$-basis of $\mathbb{C}^2$ indexed by `Fin 4` and is stable under $\iota(x)$, complexified and acting by matrix multiplication, for every $x\in\Lambda$; `hE1`, that $e\,E$ carries the relative group law `E.L` to addition; `hE2`, that $e\,E$ intertwines the action of $x\in\Lambda$ on points with multiplication by the complexified matrix $\iota(x)$; `hH1`, that every morphism $\varphi\colon E.A\to E'.A$ over the base which is a homomorphism for the group laws and commutes with the $\Lambda$-actions is given in the uniformisations by multiplication by some scalar $c\in\mathbb{C}$ with $c\cdot\mathrm{latt}(E)\subseteq\mathrm{latt}(E')$; `hH2`, the converse existence statement, that any such scalar $c$ is realised by a morphism $\varphi$ over the base which is a group-law homomorphism, is $\Lambda$-equivariant and induces multiplication by $c$; `hH3`, that a morphism over the base is determined by its effect on $\mathbb{C}$-points; `hAN`, that for every $E$, every open $U\subseteq E.A$ and every $f\in\Gamma(E.A,U)$ the set of $v\in\mathbb{C}^2$ whose associated point $e(E)^{-1}[v]$ lands in $U$ is open and the value of $f$ at that point is a holomorphic function of $v$ on this set; and `hCOV`, that near every $v_0\in\mathbb{C}^2$ two sections $f_1,f_2$ over a suitable open $U$ give a map $F$ defined on a ball $B(v_0,\varepsilon)$ whose components are the values of $f_1,f_2$ at $e(E)^{-1}[v]$ and which has an invertible complex Fréchet derivative $D$ at $v_0$.
--
--   The smooth algebraic chart. Let $S_c$ be a finite-type $\mathbb{C}$-algebra which is a domain, smooth over $\mathbb{C}$ (`hSc`), with $\operatorname{rank}_{S_c}\Omega_{S_c/\mathbb{C}}=1$ (`hΩ`); let $t\in S_c$, let $\sigma_0\colon S_c\to\mathbb{C}$ be a $\mathbb{C}$-algebra map, let $r>0$ and let $\mathcal{U}$ be a set of $\mathbb{C}$-points of $S_c$ with $\sigma_0\in\mathcal{U}$, such that $\sigma\mapsto\sigma(t)$ is a bijection of $\mathcal{U}$ onto the ball $B(\sigma_0(t),r)$ (`hbij`) and such that for every $s\in S_c$ the function $\sigma\mapsto\sigma(s)$ is of the form $F(\sigma(t))$ for some $F$ holomorphic on $B(\sigma_0(t),r)$ (`hhol`).
--
--   The family. Let $m\in\mathbb{N}$, let $\mathcal{U\!A}$ be a pair consisting of a fake elliptic curve for $(\Lambda,N)$ over $S_c$ together with a full level-$m$ structure on it (a point $P$ over the base which is $m$-torsion, generates the $m$-torsion up to the $\Lambda$-action at geometric points, and has annihilator $m\Lambda$ in $\Lambda$), let $u\colon\mathbb{C}\to$ (fake elliptic curves for $(\Lambda,N)$ over $\mathbb{C}$ with full level $m$) and let $g(z)\colon (u\,z).1.A\to\mathcal{U\!A}.1.A$. The hypothesis `hg` states that for every $\sigma\in\mathcal{U}$ the square formed by $g(\sigma(t))$, $(u(\sigma(t))).1.f$, $\mathcal{U\!A}.1.f$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\sigma$ is cartesian, and moreover that $g(\sigma(t))$ is compatible with the relative group laws on $\mathbb{C}$-points, commutes with the $\Lambda$-actions, carries points factoring through the level-$N$ morphism `lev` of the fibre to points factoring through the level-$N$ morphism of $\mathcal{U\!A}$, and satisfies $(u(\sigma(t))).2.P$ followed by $g(\sigma(t))$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\sigma$ followed by $\mathcal{U\!A}.2.P$.
--
--   The relative-analyticity data. Let $\varepsilon>0$ with $\varepsilon\le r$ and let $\kappa\colon\mathbb{C}\to\mathbb{C}$ be nonvanishing on $B(\sigma_0(t),\varepsilon)$ (`hκ`). Four further hypotheses, summarised here, govern the relative uniformisation $(z,w)\mapsto e(u\,z).1^{-1}[\kappa(z)w]$ followed by $g(z)$: `hRELAN`, that for each open $V\subseteq\mathcal{U\!A}.1.A$ and each $f\in\Gamma(\mathcal{U\!A}.1.A,V)$ the set of pairs $(\sigma(t),w)$ in $B(\sigma_0(t),\varepsilon)\times\mathbb{C}^2$ whose associated morphism lands in $V$ is open and the value of $f$ there is a holomorphic function of $(\sigma(t),w)$; `hRELCOV`, in its merged-pair form, that whenever two parameters $w_1,w_1'$ give the same morphism at $\sigma_1(t)$ there are an open $V$, two sections $f_2,f_3$ over $V$, a radius $\delta>0$, two invertible derivatives $D,D'$ and a map $\Phi$ (identity in the first coordinate, the values of $f_2,f_3$ in the second) defined on the two balls of radius $\delta$ about $(\sigma_1(t),w_1)$ and $(\sigma_1(t),w_1')$, which is differentiable with derivatives $D$ and $D'$ at these two points and whose two component values separate points, in the sense that equality of the $f_2$- and $f_3$-values at $(\sigma(t),w)$ and $(\sigma(t),w')$ forces the two associated morphisms to coincide; `hKCL`, that if $\kappa(\sigma_0(t))w\notin\mathrm{latt}(u(\sigma_0(t))).1$ then for some $\delta>0$ and all $z\in B(\sigma_0(t),\delta)$ every $w'$ with $\kappa(z)w'\in\mathrm{latt}(u\,z).1$ satisfies $\|w'-w\|\ge\delta$; and `hRELSURJ`, that points of the fibres whose values on a finite set of sections are sufficiently close to those of a given reference point are themselves of the form $e(u\,z).1^{-1}[\kappa(z)w]$ with $w$ in a prescribed ball.
--
--   The holomorphic frame. Finally let $\varepsilon'>0$ with $\varepsilon'\le\varepsilon$ and let $v_0,\dots,v_3\colon\mathbb{C}\to\mathbb{C}^2$ be holomorphic on $B(\sigma_0(t),\varepsilon')$ (`hv`) and such that (`hbasis`) for every $z$ in that ball one has $\kappa(z)v_i(z)\in\mathrm{latt}(u\,z).1$ for all $i$, and every $x\in\mathrm{latt}(u\,z).1$ has a unique expression $\kappa(z)^{-1}x=\sum_i n_i v_i(z)$ with $n\in\mathbb{Z}^4$.
--
--   Conclusion. There exist $\varepsilon''\in\mathbb{R}$, a map $A\colon\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\to\mathbb{Z}^{4\times4}$, a set $T\subseteq\mathbb{Z}^4$ and $a_0\in\mathbb{Z}^4$ with $0<\varepsilon''\le\varepsilon'$ such that, on the ball $B(\sigma_0(t),\varepsilon'')$, the following three assertions hold.
--
--   First, for every $z$ in the ball, every $\lambda\in\Lambda$ and every index $j_0$,
--   $$\big(\iota(\lambda)\text{ complexified}\big)\cdot v_{j_0}(z)=\sum_i A(\lambda)_{i\,j_0}\,v_i(z),$$
--   so the matrix of the $\Lambda$-action in the frame $v$ is independent of $z$.
--
--   Second, for every $z$ in the ball and every $w\in\mathbb{C}^2$: there exists a $\mathbb{C}$-point $P$ of $(u\,z).1$ over the base which factors through the level-$N$ morphism $(u\,z).1.\mathrm{lev}$ and satisfies $e(u\,z).1\,P=[w]$ if and only if there exists $n\in T$ with $[w]=\big[\kappa(z)\cdot N^{-1}\sum_i n_i v_i(z)\big]$ in $\mathbb{C}^2/\mathrm{latt}(u\,z).1$.
--
--   Third, for every $z$ in the ball the full level-$m$ generator satisfies
--   $$e(u\,z).1\,\big((u\,z).2.P\big)=\Big[\kappa(z)\cdot m^{-1}\sum_i (a_0)_i\,v_i(z)\Big]$$
--   in $\mathbb{C}^2/\mathrm{latt}(u\,z).1$.
--
--   Thus the integral coordinates of the quaternionic action, of the set of level-$N$ points and of the full-level generator, read in the holomorphic frame $v$, may be chosen constant in $z$ on a possibly smaller disc.
--
--   This is the local-constancy step in the analytic study of families of fake elliptic curves with full level structure over a smooth algebraic chart: the three pieces of discrete data (the matrices of the maximal order acting on the period frame, the level-$N$ points, and the level-$m$ generator) vary continuously in the parameter while taking values in discrete sets, hence are constant on a disc. It combines the three companion results on constancy of the $\Lambda$-action, of the level structure and of the generator, and is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.exists_holomorphic_latticeFrame_of_analytic_of_smooth_algebraicChart`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.exists_holomorphic_latticeFrame_of_analytic_of_smooth_algebraicChart) and its variant without a coprimality assumption.
